WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.883
Things move when you push
them, or when you pull them.

2
00:00:08.103 --> 00:00:11.447
And in water, some things
float, and some things sink.

3
00:00:11.947 --> 00:00:16.033
A push moves something away from
you. Kicking a ball is a push.

4
00:00:16.253 --> 00:00:20.572
A pull moves something towards
you. Opening a drawer is a pull.

5
00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:25.994
A push does not have to be hard. A
gentle tap on a doorbell is still a push.

6
00:00:26.214 --> 00:00:31.601
Pushes and pulls are forces. A force
can make a thing move, stop or turn.

7
00:00:32.101 --> 00:00:37.627
This track is marked in steps. We count
the steps to measure how far it rolls.

8
00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:43.002
Push it gently, and it rolls a
little way. One, two, three steps.

9
00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:47.169
Now push it hard. It rolls a long
way, all the way to nine steps!

10
00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:51.940
Same ball, same floor. The only
thing that changed was the push.

11
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.804
So a bigger push makes a bigger
move. Three steps, then nine!

12
00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:02.180
A ball on the floor stays still. Round
things do not move by themselves.

13
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.069
A push starts it moving. Now
the ball is rolling along.

14
00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:10.237
Put your hand in front and
push back. The ball stops.

15
00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:14.172
Tap the rolling ball on the side.
It turns and goes a new way.

16
00:01:14.392 --> 00:01:17.875
So a push can start a thing,
stop it, or make it turn.

17
00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:21.718
Drop an apple into the
water. It floats on the top.

18
00:01:21.938 --> 00:01:25.329
Drop a stone into the water.
It sinks to the bottom.

19
00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:30.007
You cannot always tell by looking.
Will this big log float or sink?

20
00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:36.218
Predict first: say what you think will
happen. Then drop it in. The big log floats!

21
00:01:36.438 --> 00:01:40.571
A tiny coin sinks. So do not
guess. You have to test it.

22
00:01:41.071 --> 00:01:44.647
A bicycle moves because your
feet push the pedals round.

23
00:01:44.867 --> 00:01:49.046
Your hands pull the brakes to
stop. Push to go, pull to stop.

24
00:01:49.266 --> 00:01:52.331
A boat floats because the
water pushes up on it.

25
00:01:52.551 --> 00:01:56.174
The wind pushes a kite up.
The string pulls it back.

26
00:01:56.394 --> 00:01:59.133
Pushes and pulls are inside
everything that moves.

27
00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:05.020
So now you know. A push moves things
away. A pull moves them towards you.

28
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:10.210
A bigger push makes a bigger move. A
push can start, stop or turn a ball.

29
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:15.306
Some things float, and some things
sink. You have to test them to find out.

30
00:02:15.526 --> 00:02:19.148
Pushes and pulls are all around
you. Go and find some at home!
